course: dictionary
lesson: 15556
title: Supplant: taking someone's place
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To supplant something is to take its place, usually because the new thing is newer or better. The old thing is pushed out of its position. «Computers supplanted typewriters in most offices.» The new machines did the job, so the typewriters were replaced.
explain: Supplant can also mean to push someone out of their position, sometimes by tricks. «The clever servant tried to supplant the trusted adviser by telling lies.» The clues are telling lies and tried to, so the servant wanted the adviser's job and did not play fair.
explain: Supplant is a formal word, so you will meet it in history, science and the news. Look for two things in the sentence: an old thing or person, and a new one that takes over. To check your meaning, swap in "took the place of" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Supplant means to take someone's or something's place.
fact: Supplant is often used when something newer or better takes over from something older.
fact: Supplant can also mean to push someone out of their position, sometimes by tricks.
fact: Supplant is a formal word: you will find it in history books, science writing and the news.
fact: Phrases: «be supplanted by» means "be replaced by", as in «The old method was supplanted by a new one.»
exercise: «Computers supplanted typewriters in most offices.» What does supplanted mean here? | Were sold in shops | Helped to type faster | Broke into pieces | *Took the place of
exercise: Ella says supplant means "to help". What does it really mean? | *To take someone's place | To help someone up | To sing loudly | To wait patiently
exercise: «The new phone model will supplant the old one next year.» What happens? | *The new model takes the old one's place | The old model is painted red | Nothing changes at all | The new model is given away free
test: What does supplant mean in «He tried to supplant his boss by lying»? | Work beside his boss | Thank his boss for the help | Give his boss a present | *Push his boss out of the job, by trickery
test: Which phrase means the same as "be supplanted by"? | Be painted by | Be loved by | *Be replaced by | Be hidden by
exam: In the Bible story, «Jacob supplanted his brother Esau.» What does this mean? | *Jacob took Esau's place by trickery | Jacob and Esau went hunting together | Jacob gave Esau a gift | Esau took Jacob's place as a shepherd
